A group of friends and I went
up to a waterfall one Saturday

00:41:32.506 --> 00:41:35.180
and I was not being particularly wise

00:41:35.180 --> 00:41:38.653
as I was walking on some
rocks on top of a waterfall.

00:41:38.653 --> 00:41:41.145
So of course, I slipped
and I fell on my stomach

00:41:41.145 --> 00:41:44.712
down one small waterfall and then another,

00:41:44.712 --> 00:41:46.811
until I fortunately, landed in a pool

00:41:46.811 --> 00:41:48.679
deep enough to stop me,

00:41:48.679 --> 00:41:51.801
about a small cars width
from a 50-foot drop

00:41:51.801 --> 00:41:53.801
to just a pile of rocks.

00:41:54.812 --> 00:41:56.913
To make matters worse,
The pool I landed in

00:41:56.913 --> 00:42:00.219
was full of leeches and
they were all over my legs,

00:42:00.219 --> 00:42:01.857
all the way up my swimsuit.

00:42:01.857 --> 00:42:02.690
Oh.

00:42:02.690 --> 00:42:03.523
And one last thing,

00:42:03.523 --> 00:42:05.895
I was with a group of friends
from a campus ministry

00:42:05.895 --> 00:42:07.284
I was in at the time,

00:42:07.284 --> 00:42:09.901
I have a similar
deconstruction story to y'alls.

00:42:09.901 --> 00:42:12.872
And the guy that helped
pick the leeches off my legs

00:42:12.872 --> 00:42:15.668
kept complaining about how weird it was

00:42:15.668 --> 00:42:17.978
and how uncomfortable it made him.

00:42:17.978 --> 00:42:20.170
So that was a great Saturday.

00:42:20.170 --> 00:42:21.003
Yeah.

00:42:21.003 --> 00:42:23.893
That, getting a little homoerotic there.

00:42:23.893 --> 00:42:26.002
Little uncomfortable for the...

00:42:26.002 --> 00:42:27.644
Is that what was happening?

00:42:27.644 --> 00:42:28.542
I think it was,

00:42:28.542 --> 00:42:29.394
it was just like, oh.

00:42:29.394 --> 00:42:30.843
No, I just kind of think pulling leeches

00:42:30.843 --> 00:42:32.786
off somebody is weird.

00:42:32.786 --> 00:42:36.623
Spirituality aside, like
belief system aside.

00:42:36.623 --> 00:42:38.980
I think, my understanding was why

00:42:38.980 --> 00:42:40.256
he would made the connection

00:42:40.256 --> 00:42:41.526
is if the guy was a little uncomfortable

00:42:41.526 --> 00:42:43.432
with getting close to
his junk or something.

00:42:43.432 --> 00:42:45.493
Dude, freaking going off of a water.

00:42:45.493 --> 00:42:47.548
You gotta be freaking careful, man.

00:42:47.548 --> 00:42:49.521
If you're like hanging
out around a waterfall

00:42:49.521 --> 00:42:52.613
and if you're in the
water that then starts to

00:42:52.613 --> 00:42:54.470
eventually falls.

00:42:54.470 --> 00:42:56.027
It's just not a good practice.

00:42:56.027 --> 00:43:01.027
You don't wanna be in
pre-waterfall water, you know?

00:43:01.099 --> 00:43:02.257
Yeah.

00:43:02.257 --> 00:43:05.469
It just seems like something to live by.

00:43:05.469 --> 00:43:07.135
I don't swim in pre-waterfall water.

00:43:07.135 --> 00:43:11.465
The most visceral this
has ever been for me

00:43:11.465 --> 00:43:14.768
was when we visited Niagara Falls.

00:43:14.768 --> 00:43:17.190
And so there's been
plenty of times in my life

00:43:17.190 --> 00:43:19.751
when I've been like in
a creek or in a river

00:43:19.751 --> 00:43:21.949
that had a waterfall and
you're like kind of swimming

00:43:21.949 --> 00:43:23.382
and you're like, I'm not gonna go there

00:43:23.382 --> 00:43:25.004
because it's a waterfall.
Yeah.

00:43:25.004 --> 00:43:27.651
But one time we were swimming at Yosemite

00:43:27.651 --> 00:43:29.419
when I was a kid.

00:43:29.419 --> 00:43:32.178
I remember this very clearly
because my dad was like,

00:43:32.178 --> 00:43:33.914
"There's a waterfall down there."

00:43:33.914 --> 00:43:36.226
And then years later we heard about people

00:43:36.226 --> 00:43:37.429
who would be swimming in Yosemite

00:43:37.429 --> 00:43:40.150
and get swept down and go off
a giant waterfall and die.

00:43:40.150 --> 00:43:40.983
Yeah.

00:43:40.983 --> 00:43:42.909
The year that I was
there, we hiked to the top

00:43:42.909 --> 00:43:46.395
of Yosemite Falls and they
were doing a helicopter rescue

00:43:46.395 --> 00:43:48.549
of someone who had gone over the falls.

00:43:48.549 --> 00:43:49.613
Yeah.

00:43:49.613 --> 00:43:50.929
But when we went to Niagara falls,

00:43:50.929 --> 00:43:52.995
when we visited Niagara
falls with our wives.

00:43:52.995 --> 00:43:54.328
Yeah.

00:43:54.328 --> 00:43:57.598
And we were on the Canadian side.

00:43:57.598 --> 00:43:58.431
Right?

00:43:58.431 --> 00:43:59.756
Which is the better side.

00:43:59.756 --> 00:44:03.093
Nothing against America, but
just, it's a cooler side.

00:44:03.093 --> 00:44:04.441
More picturesque, I believe.

00:44:04.441 --> 00:44:05.691
Of the river.

00:44:07.908 --> 00:44:08.808
It's crazy.

00:44:08.808 --> 00:44:10.630
You can get right down there next to 'em.

00:44:10.630 --> 00:44:12.377
You can't really if I remember correctly,

00:44:12.377 --> 00:44:14.760
you can't like walk to it or
whatever, if you're just a,

00:44:14.760 --> 00:44:17.677
you know, a civilian, but obviously

00:44:18.910 --> 00:44:20.652
you don't want to go off Niagara Falls.

00:44:20.652 --> 00:44:25.541
And just the other day I
saw a video going around,

00:44:25.541 --> 00:44:26.404
I think on Twitter.

00:44:26.404 --> 00:44:29.754
And it was the guy who cuts the grass.

00:44:29.754 --> 00:44:30.587
What?

00:44:30.587 --> 00:44:32.395
Above the Falls.

00:44:32.395 --> 00:44:35.062
And he's got a rope tied to him.

00:44:36.142 --> 00:44:38.476
So like the person who's
like mowing the grass.

00:44:38.476 --> 00:44:40.109
Is he on a riding lawnmower?

00:44:40.109 --> 00:44:40.942
with a rope attached to him?

00:44:40.942 --> 00:44:41.852
In my mind he had a push mower

00:44:41.852 --> 00:44:45.952
because it was a place
you didn't wanna be like

00:44:45.952 --> 00:44:47.512
on a vehicle that could fall in.

00:44:47.512 --> 00:44:49.477
It was just like, Okay, I'm
kind of mowing the grass here."

00:44:49.477 --> 00:44:50.310
Oh wow.

00:44:50.310 --> 00:44:52.227
"And I'm buckled in."

00:44:53.635 --> 00:44:54.468
Here we go.

00:44:54.468 --> 00:44:55.301
There you go.

00:44:55.301 --> 00:44:57.301
There he is right there.

00:44:58.576 --> 00:45:00.826
Dude, using a push mower.

00:45:00.826 --> 00:45:02.756
And he is got like this giant-

00:45:02.756 --> 00:45:03.589
Yeah.

00:45:03.589 --> 00:45:05.596
That makes sense.
Harness around him.

00:45:05.596 --> 00:45:07.281
And a sleeveless shirt.

00:45:07.281 --> 00:45:08.492
Well, you don't want to be weighed down.

00:45:08.492 --> 00:45:11.559
I think he's just wearing...

00:45:11.559 --> 00:45:13.703
That's a mow job I don't want.

00:45:13.703 --> 00:45:15.286
Really?

00:45:15.286 --> 00:45:17.710
Extra challenging though.

00:45:17.710 --> 00:45:18.543
That's beautiful though.

00:45:18.543 --> 00:45:19.817
That's advanced mowing.

00:45:19.817 --> 00:45:20.666
People go, yeah.

00:45:20.666 --> 00:45:23.104
There was the person who drove their car

00:45:23.104 --> 00:45:25.945
and was like the car
with the person in it,

00:45:25.945 --> 00:45:28.678
was like close to the
edge of Niagara Falls,

00:45:28.678 --> 00:45:30.710
like a few months ago.

00:45:30.710 --> 00:45:32.205
And they had to do a
rescue to get the person

00:45:32.205 --> 00:45:33.203
out of the car.

00:45:33.203 --> 00:45:34.081
They were in the water?

00:45:34.081 --> 00:45:35.218
Yeah.

00:45:35.218 --> 00:45:36.051
Yeah.

00:45:37.047 --> 00:45:37.880
And yeah.

00:45:37.880 --> 00:45:39.685
I guess if your car is up there
don't get out of your car.

00:45:39.685 --> 00:45:42.225
I don't think they were conscious.

00:45:42.225 --> 00:45:43.937
'Cause then you're in serious trouble.

00:45:43.937 --> 00:45:44.770
Good gracious.

00:45:44.770 --> 00:45:46.032
I mean, yeah.

00:45:46.032 --> 00:45:49.753
Imagine going over a
waterfall landing in a pool

00:45:49.753 --> 00:45:52.938
and then struggling, but
then Jacob went over again,

00:45:52.938 --> 00:45:54.546
landing in a second pool

00:45:54.546 --> 00:45:56.197
and then he finally got it together.

00:45:56.197 --> 00:45:57.570
'Cause if he'd gone over that third one

00:45:57.570 --> 00:46:01.876
he would've been in a
thousand pieces, man.

00:46:01.876 --> 00:46:04.083
Well, and then yeah, pool full of leeches

00:46:04.083 --> 00:46:07.035
and a uncomfortable moment with a friend.

00:46:07.035 --> 00:46:08.226
Man.

00:46:08.226 --> 00:46:13.147
My bizarre near-death experience happened

00:46:13.147 --> 00:46:16.897
when I had to get foot
surgery on my big toe.

00:46:19.750 --> 00:46:24.750
They thought it was a bone
infection or something like that.

00:46:25.715 --> 00:46:29.746
So went in for the surgery
at an outpatient center,

00:46:29.746 --> 00:46:33.294
proceeded to apparently
go into anaphylactic shock

00:46:33.294 --> 00:46:37.943
on the table, allergic to
some of the medications

00:46:37.943 --> 00:46:40.621
they gave me for the surgery.

00:46:40.621 --> 00:46:43.253
I woke up, was told about it

00:46:43.253 --> 00:46:48.253
and I was the outpatient
center's first code blue ever.

00:46:48.562 --> 00:46:51.691
So that is my bizarre
near-death experience

00:46:51.691 --> 00:46:54.686
that my big toe tried to kill me.

00:46:54.686 --> 00:46:55.519
Dang.

00:46:55.519 --> 00:46:56.608
I mean, that's scary.

00:46:56.608 --> 00:46:58.079
'Cause this is a group of doctors

00:46:58.079 --> 00:47:01.337
who are not accustomed
necessarily to dealing with-

00:47:01.337 --> 00:47:02.170
Outpatients.

00:47:02.170 --> 00:47:05.195
Yeah.
You know, code blue.

00:47:05.195 --> 00:47:06.028
Yeah.

00:47:06.028 --> 00:47:07.184
It's like, we're just gonna
take care of your toe.

00:47:07.184 --> 00:47:08.423
I mean just makes me think.

00:47:08.423 --> 00:47:11.314
Every time they ask me, "Are
you allergic to anything?"

00:47:11.314 --> 00:47:13.161
It's just like, I always brush it off.

00:47:13.161 --> 00:47:15.093
"Of course not, pollen?"

00:47:15.093 --> 00:47:17.361
When I was little, my mom would say,

00:47:17.361 --> 00:47:21.361
"He's allergic to amoxicillin
because as a baby,

00:47:22.359 --> 00:47:25.370
he had a little reaction to it."

00:47:25.370 --> 00:47:28.585
But then at a certain point,
I just stopped saying that.

00:47:28.585 --> 00:47:30.762
Well, when was the time
you had antibiotics?

00:47:30.762 --> 00:47:32.012
I don't know.

00:47:33.039 --> 00:47:33.956
Many years.

00:47:34.825 --> 00:47:35.807
'Cause I mean, there's still
a big class of antibiotics.

00:47:35.807 --> 00:47:37.732
Maybe ten years.

00:47:37.732 --> 00:47:39.847
I mean, it might be worth finding out.

00:47:39.847 --> 00:47:42.619
But usually what will happen
is you're not gonna die.

00:47:42.619 --> 00:47:45.019
Like you'll be in like
the first or second day

00:47:45.019 --> 00:47:46.542
of taking them usually.

00:47:46.542 --> 00:47:48.993
And then you'll be like,
this happens to Jesse.

00:47:48.993 --> 00:47:51.371
She'd be like, "Oh I'm reacting to this."

00:47:51.371 --> 00:47:52.204
Yeah.

00:47:52.204 --> 00:47:56.064
And then you just stop
and get on another one.

00:47:56.064 --> 00:47:56.897
I had toe surgery.

00:47:56.897 --> 00:47:59.556
It's the only surgery I've ever had.

00:47:59.556 --> 00:48:02.314
When you broke your toe
after the basketball game.

00:48:02.314 --> 00:48:04.647
No, ingrown toenail.

00:48:04.647 --> 00:48:06.230
Oh, you got that?

00:48:07.443 --> 00:48:11.613
I had an ingrown toenail in high school

00:48:11.613 --> 00:48:14.726
and went to the podiatrist
and still the one of the toe,

00:48:14.726 --> 00:48:16.433
I got some messed up toenails in general,

00:48:16.433 --> 00:48:19.288
but one of 'em on my big toe.

00:48:19.288 --> 00:48:22.289
Like you can kind of
tell that what they do

00:48:22.289 --> 00:48:24.257
is so that it...

00:48:24.257 --> 00:48:26.037
One side of, one of my big toes.

00:48:26.037 --> 00:48:27.293
Oh no.

00:48:27.293 --> 00:48:29.180
Doesn't go under the skin.

00:48:29.180 --> 00:48:31.763
The nail doesn't meet the skin.

00:48:33.521 --> 00:48:34.991
You gotta learn how to scuba dive

00:48:34.991 --> 00:48:37.300
and you gotta take this
kind of stuff, man.

00:48:37.300 --> 00:48:38.853
And so they did something
where they like cut it

00:48:38.853 --> 00:48:41.653
so that it would, and I was fully awake

00:48:41.653 --> 00:48:44.017
and it was just like numbed or whatever,

00:48:44.017 --> 00:48:45.767
no code blues for me.

00:48:46.875 --> 00:48:49.196
But yeah, that's the one surgery
I've had, is toe surgery.

00:48:49.196 --> 00:48:50.029
Big toe surgery.

00:48:50.029 --> 00:48:50.908
That's what we've got in common.

00:48:50.908 --> 00:48:53.789
It's so interesting to wake
up from an outpatient surgery

00:48:53.789 --> 00:48:57.093
and they say, "Oh, you died for a second."

00:48:57.093 --> 00:48:58.807
It's like, "What?"

00:48:58.807 --> 00:49:00.919
Like, "My toe died for a second?

00:49:00.919 --> 00:49:01.752
No, you died for a second."

00:49:01.752 --> 00:49:05.502
Well, this is kind of
crazy, for two reasons.

00:49:06.371 --> 00:49:09.566
Two things that I've
been looking into lately,

00:49:09.566 --> 00:49:14.531
the first is I just happened
to see a article yesterday.

00:49:14.531 --> 00:49:17.951
And it was like a collection of people

00:49:17.951 --> 00:49:20.653
who woke up during
surgery and their stories.

00:49:20.653 --> 00:49:21.798
God.

00:49:21.798 --> 00:49:24.925
See, I wonder if we're
gonna get the numbers back

00:49:24.925 --> 00:49:27.440
on this episode and be
like, "No one's listening

00:49:27.440 --> 00:49:29.740
to this episode 'cause
they're smarter than I am."

00:49:29.740 --> 00:49:30.573
No.

00:49:30.573 --> 00:49:32.758
I didn't realize that I
didn't want to hear this.

00:49:32.758 --> 00:49:35.261
Well, here's the thing, you
don't like Chainsaw Man,

00:49:35.261 --> 00:49:36.778
but there's a market for it.

00:49:36.778 --> 00:49:37.611
Okay.

00:49:37.611 --> 00:49:38.444
I'm in the market for it.

00:49:38.444 --> 00:49:39.572
And I'm speaking right now.

00:49:39.572 --> 00:49:43.630
Why are you reading about
people waking up during surgery?

00:49:43.630 --> 00:49:45.384
'Cause I have a fear of that happening.

00:49:45.384 --> 00:49:47.152
But then why read about it?

00:49:47.152 --> 00:49:49.236
To know how bad it's
gonna be, to be prepared.

00:49:49.236 --> 00:49:51.511
So you're convinced it's
gonna happen to you.

00:49:51.511 --> 00:49:53.221
It wasn't as bad as I...

00:49:53.221 --> 00:49:54.983
I mean, there was a couple
people who were like,

00:49:54.983 --> 00:49:56.731
"It was the worst pain
I've ever experienced.

00:49:56.731 --> 00:49:58.681
Nothing has ever come close."

00:49:58.681 --> 00:50:00.531
But there was a couple people
who were like, "I woke up,

00:50:00.531 --> 00:50:03.337
everybody saw me, they
gave me a little bit more

00:50:03.337 --> 00:50:07.144
of the juice and I went back to sleep."

00:50:07.144 --> 00:50:08.609
I won't go into any
more details about that.

00:50:08.609 --> 00:50:09.909
But the second thing
I've been reading about-

00:50:09.909 --> 00:50:12.496
So you're telling me
it made you feel better

00:50:12.496 --> 00:50:13.660
reading about those things.

00:50:13.660 --> 00:50:15.160
I feel the same.

00:50:16.856 --> 00:50:18.151
The second thing I've been reading about,

00:50:18.151 --> 00:50:22.901
and I find it interesting that
we didn't get any of these

00:50:23.864 --> 00:50:27.346
and Daniel is it that
we didn't get any at all

00:50:27.346 --> 00:50:29.768
or that they're not in these
ones that we're selecting from

00:50:29.768 --> 00:50:32.156
in terms of people who
actually like saw something.

00:50:32.156 --> 00:50:32.989
Like saw the light?

00:50:32.989 --> 00:50:34.526
Saw the light.

00:50:34.526 --> 00:50:35.359
Okay.

00:50:35.359 --> 00:50:40.359
No one in the Mythical Beast
community has seen the light.

00:50:40.980 --> 00:50:45.307
And I wouldn't say that I am like going,

00:50:45.307 --> 00:50:48.972
I haven't gone hardcore
like deep into this,

00:50:48.972 --> 00:50:53.055
but I'm finding myself
reading about and watching

00:50:54.314 --> 00:50:57.669
documentaries about people's
near-death experiences

00:50:57.669 --> 00:51:00.303
and actually experiencing
like out of body stuff.

00:51:00.303 --> 00:51:02.217
I mean, I still don't know
what I think about it.

00:51:02.217 --> 00:51:03.967
I'm in an open place.

00:51:04.809 --> 00:51:06.645
Is it like, okay, this is just something

00:51:06.645 --> 00:51:08.856
where there's like DMT
released in your brain

00:51:08.856 --> 00:51:12.467
when you die and you feel
like this is what's happening?

00:51:12.467 --> 00:51:13.742
Yeah.

00:51:13.742 --> 00:51:15.608
But it's pretty fascinating how...

00:51:15.608 --> 00:51:19.088
I was actually hoping we would
get some of those submissions

00:51:19.088 --> 00:51:20.412
based on some of the
stuff I've been reading,

00:51:20.412 --> 00:51:22.881
'Cause they are relatively common

00:51:22.881 --> 00:51:26.704
and there's all these
scientists, you know,

00:51:26.704 --> 00:51:29.041
people who had like a
completely materialistic,

00:51:29.041 --> 00:51:30.423
naturalistic view of the world

00:51:30.423 --> 00:51:32.360
where they're like, "Consciousness

00:51:32.360 --> 00:51:34.514
is completely contained in the mind."

00:51:34.514 --> 00:51:36.896
Who basically began looking into this

00:51:36.896 --> 00:51:40.687
and were like, "I can't
in good conscience,

00:51:40.687 --> 00:51:42.723
continue to believe that that's the case.

00:51:42.723 --> 00:51:45.326
Something else must be going
on with all these things

00:51:45.326 --> 00:51:46.615
that are happening to people."

00:51:46.615 --> 00:51:48.520
And of course, this is not anything new

00:51:48.520 --> 00:51:49.739
people have been talking
about this forever,

00:51:49.739 --> 00:51:51.156
but I don't know.

00:51:52.246 --> 00:51:53.583
It was a little intriguing.

00:51:53.583 --> 00:51:57.004
My granddad, so my mom's dad, you know,

00:51:57.004 --> 00:51:58.921
he passed away in 1996.

00:52:00.005 --> 00:52:00.883
Oh, I remember that.

00:52:00.883 --> 00:52:05.883
I mean, he had two separate
open heart surgery procedures,

00:52:08.564 --> 00:52:11.936
like where they split you
open, at least back then,

00:52:11.936 --> 00:52:14.353
from sternum down your thigh.

00:52:18.269 --> 00:52:21.836
The scar that he had is just
like crazy train tracks.

00:52:21.836 --> 00:52:23.299
Why do they have to go so deep?

00:52:23.299 --> 00:52:25.098
I don't know.

00:52:25.098 --> 00:52:27.940
It's like trying to open a
book and you really just gotta.

00:52:27.940 --> 00:52:28.852
You gotta keep ripping it.

00:52:28.852 --> 00:52:29.685
Yeah, right.

00:52:29.685 --> 00:52:30.743
You gotta keep ripping.

00:52:30.743 --> 00:52:32.158
